 {
  "id": "tp-ncert-chem-11-ch06-011",
  "subject": "chemistry",
  "chapter": "thermodynamics",
  "source": {
   "type": "third-party",
   "name": "NCERT Exemplar 11",
   "year": 0,
   "version": "",
   "number": 11,
   "file": "sources/third-party/chemistry/ncert-exemplar-11/keep506.pdf",
   "page": 3,
   "key_file": "sources/third-party/chemistry/ncert-exemplar-11/keep506.pdf"
  },
  "stem": "Consider the reactions given below. On the basis of these reactions find out which of the algebric relations given in options (i) to (iv) is correct?\n\n(a) $\\mathrm{C(g) + 4H(g) \\rightarrow CH_4(g)}$; $\\Delta_rH = x\\,\\mathrm{kJ\\,mol^{-1}}$\n\n(b) $\\mathrm{C(graphite,s) + 2H_2(g) \\rightarrow CH_4(g)}$; $\\Delta_rH = y\\,\\mathrm{kJ\\,mol^{-1}}$",
  "options": [
   "$x = y$",
   "$x = 2y$",
   "$x > y$",
   "$x < y$"
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "accepted": [
   3
  ],
  "images": [],
  "status": "verified",
  "in_syllabus": true,
  "checks": {
   "key_official": false,
   "blind_haiku": 3,
   "verify": "disputed",
   "notes": "Key (iii) x>y read correctly from image; but (a) is reverse atomisation of CH4 (about -1665 kJ/mol) vs formation y (about -75), so x<y; printed key justification only holds for magnitudes.",
   "key_override": {
    "reason": "The printed options (i) x=y (ii) x=2y (iii) x>y (iv) x<y are transcribed correctly and the book's ANSWERS page gives 11. (iii), but that key is wrong for signed Delta_rH values: reaction (a) needs no bond broken while (b) must break 2 H-H bonds, so (a) is far more exothermic and x is the more negative number, i.e. x < y. The book's own justification ('bonds between reactant molecules are broken only in reaction (b)') points the same way; (iii) holds only for magnitudes.",
    "published_key": [
     2
    ]
   },
   "solver_agrees": [
    "haiku",
    "sonnet"
   ]
  }
 },
